# Every service Dockerfile builds with context `../..` (repo root, see
# deploy/homelab/docker-compose.yml) and COPYs only pyproject.toml,
# uv.lock, shared/, its own services/<name>/, and (reachy-hub only)
# clients/web-pwa/. With no .dockerignore at all, every `docker compose
# build` shipped the *entire* repo to the Docker daemon as build context
# on every single build — including .venv (~1.6GB) and .git — before a
# single COPY instruction even ran. That was almost certainly the
# dominant cost in "docker compose takes a long time," not apt/uv
# download time. None of the paths below are referenced by any
# Dockerfile's COPY list.

.venv/
**/.venv/
.git/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
**/*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
vendor/
docs/
.claude/
# Deployment credentials and the SecretStore keyring must never enter build context.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Phase 47A: the web client is built inside the image's Node stage from source.
# Host-side installs and builds must not enter the context or shadow that build.
clients/web/node_modules/
clients/web/dist/
clients/web/test-results/
clients/web/playwright-report/
